---
const tags = [
  "no proxy",
  "no DNS changes",
  "<10 ms per evaluation",
  "402 + HATEOAS native",
];
---

<div class="px-6 py-24 text-center sm:py-28">
  <div class="eyebrow">Sidecar middleware for APIs</div>
  <h1
    class="mx-auto mt-7 font-bold tracking-tight text-ink"
    style="font-size: clamp(46px, 8vw, 84px); line-height: 1.03; letter-spacing: -0.045em;"
  >
    A bouncer<br /><span style="color:#6f6d68">for your API.</span>
  </h1>
  <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-[680px] text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
    bufferq runs as a sidecar middleware next to your API — no proxy, no DNS
    changes. It works out who's actually calling: human, script, or autonomous
    agent. Then it decides to let them through, grant them a slot, or queue them
    with a token to come back. 402 native and HATEOAS native for better
    understanding from agents.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
    <a class="btn btn-dark" href="#">Get started</a>
    <a class="btn btn-line" href="#flow">See the flow</a>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
    {tags.map((t) => <span class="pill-tag">{t}</span>)}
  </div>
</div>
